		"Name": "Fireball",
		"Details": "Captured Fireball salvage from the Federated Suns had a tall order in the Capellan Confederation. The design was not well liked by Capellan MechWarriors and the Confederation's scouting role was covered by other 'Mechs. However, a Warrior House Imarra MechTech had an inspired idea, based on the well-known UrbanMech UM-R29: mount a COIL to it and use it as a last-ditch one-shot wonder. The plan was approved and the ALM-7L entered service shortly thereafter. Armed with exclusively a COIL, the -7L uses a smaller engine than the source -7D does, taken from spare Locust chassis. The COIL is a tremendously dangerous weapon but the -7L can only use it sparingly, lest the waste heat melt the frame. Pilots assigned to the -7L often complain about the assignment... until their first mission when they rarely come home.\n\n <b><color=#e51717>COMMUNITY CONTENT</color></b>",
		"Icon": "uixTxrIcon_fireball"
	},
